/-!
# Physical monodromy in the actual specialization marking

For arbitrary holomorphic cusp data, every sufficiently small nonzero
complex level admits one original-radius four-period marking with two
proved properties: it identifies the independently prescribed collapse
with the marked specialization map up to an actual homotopy, and its
`M₀` self-map is the endpoint of jointly continuous transport around the
actual positive base circle.  All intermediate maps are homeomorphisms
between literal fibres of the original quotient.

The common small radius and all auxiliary drift estimates are derived
from the original holomorphic data.  The marking works simultaneously
for all containing closed-tube radii and all integral homology degrees.
-/
